calc=head.replace('Growth Element — Growth, unblocked.','Buy back your time — Growth Element')+nav+'''<main class="container calc-page"><div class="calc-intro"><a class="back" href="index.html">← Back to Growth Element</a><span class="kicker">THE BUY-BACK CALCULATOR</span><h1>Make room<br>for <em>what’s next.</em></h1><p>What is a repeating task costing your team? Set your own assumptions and see the capacity you could recover.</p><div class="capacity-use"><span class="kicker">WHAT WOULD YOU DO WITH THAT TIME?</span><div class="aspiration"><button class="selected" aria-pressed="true" data-goal="growth">Grow the business</button><button aria-pressed="false" data-goal="creative">Make something new</button><button aria-pressed="false" data-goal="life">Finish work earlier</button></div><p id="goalText">More space for customer conversations, follow-ups and the decisions only you can make.</p></div></div><div class="calculator"><label for="task">What work keeps repeating?</label><input id="task" placeholder="e.g. weekly sales reports" maxlength="160"><div class="formrow"><div><label for="peopleCount">People doing the task</label><input id="peopleCount" type="number" min="1" max="500" value="2"></div><div><label for="hourlyRate">Value of an hour (USD)</label><input id="hourlyRate" type="number" min="0" max="10000" value="50"></div></div><label for="weeklyHours">Hours per person / week <b id="hoursLabel">5 h</b></label><input id="weeklyHours" type="range" min="0" max="40" step="0.5" value="5"><label for="reduction">How much of this work could be reduced? <b id="reductionLabel">30%</b></label><input id="reduction" type="range" min="0" max="80" step="5" value="30"><section class="savings-panel" aria-label="Estimated savings"><div class="savings-header"><h2>Your potential savings</h2><div class="period-switch" role="group" aria-label="Savings period"><button type="button" data-period="week" aria-pressed="false">Week</button><button type="button" data-period="month" aria-pressed="true">Month</button><button type="button" data-period="year" aria-pressed="false">Year</button></div></div><div class="calc-result" aria-live="polite"><div><span class="result-label">TIME SAVED</span><strong id="weeklySaved">13 hours</strong><span id="timePeriod">each month</span></div><div><span class="result-label">VALUE OF TIME SAVED</span><strong id="monthlyValue">$650</strong><span id="moneyPeriod">each month</span></div></div><p id="annualTime" class="annual">That’s 156 hours and $7,800 worth of time over a year.</p><div class="before-after"><div><span>TIME SPENT NOW</span><b id="timeBefore">43.3 hours / month</b></div><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><div><span>TIME AFTER REDUCTION</span><b id="timeAfter">30.3 hours / month</b></div></div><p class="savings-note">An estimate based on your inputs. Dollar value reflects time freed up, not guaranteed cash savings. Costs excluded.</p></section><details><summary>Show assumptions and calculation</summary><p>People × hours per person × reduction = potential weekly capacity. Weekly capacity × 52 ÷ 12 × hourly value = monthly capacity value.</p><p>The reduction is a scenario you choose, not an AI prediction. Capacity value is not guaranteed cash savings or additional revenue. Implementation, tools, maintenance and oversight costs are excluded. A workflow review checks what is realistic.</p></details><button class="button" id="discussCalc">Talk through this workflow</button><p class="micro">No email required. Inputs stay in this browser.</p></div></main>'''+footer+modal+script
(d/'calc.html').write_text(finalize(calc,'calc.html'))
review=head.replace('Growth Element — Growth, unblocked.','Consolidation review — Growth Element')+nav+'''<main class="container review-page"><a class="back" href="index.html">← Open the consolidated site</a><span class="kicker">OCTOBER 25 / MEETING-BASED CONSOLIDATION</span><h1>Your decisions.<br><em>One website.</em></h1><p class="review-intro">Built from the Gemini transcript, with particular attention to 01:28–02:08. Later decisions take precedence over earlier brainstorming and the automatic summary.</p><a class="quietlink" href="https://docs.google.com/document/d/1r28KA7QsIFuITCrBXBOGgIhXz-0l8LxZRIuWakUKjEM/edit" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open the source meeting notes</a><div class="review-actions"><a class="button" href="index.html">Review the consolidated page</a><a class="button secondary" href="concepts.html">View the original three concepts</a></div><h2>What made the cut</h2><div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Decision implemented</th><th>Transcript</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Main headline</td><td>Keep “Grow faster, spend less, and tell a story people remember.”</td><td>01:28–01:35</td></tr><tr><td>Hero interaction</td><td>Use the outcome concept’s three growth blockers. Each card turns green and reveals the concrete approach inside the same card. No claim that clicking solves the problem.</td><td>01:57–01:59</td></tr><tr><td>Service layout</td><td>Use the first ChatGPT concept’s compact three columns and word density. Stack on mobile. Remove the redundant section eyebrow/headline.</td><td>01:41; 01:45–01:47; 02:06</td></tr><tr><td>Brand column</td><td>Keep “Stories that raise, launch and sell.” New e-commerce and AI headlines are proposed copy, not transcript-approved quotes.</td><td>01:35; 01:41</td></tr><tr><td>Supporting copy</td><td>Reuse “Stores that are easier to buy from,” “AI that takes repetitive work off your plate,” and the three concise transformation pairs.</td><td>01:51–01:54</td></tr><tr><td>Motion</td><td>Replace the vague sphere and orbit with contained input-to-output illustrations ending in a check. Include pause and reduced-motion support.</td><td>01:47–01:49; 01:53</td></tr><tr><td>Visual identity</td><td>Forest green, white and lime palette, refined after screenshot feedback; periodic-element monogram. Avoid the rejected beige newspaper look and black/gold direction.</td><td>01:44; 01:59; 02:03</td></tr><tr><td>Proof</td><td>Seven supplied logos in a static strip, labeled as the team’s previous work. Keep $3B+ tied specifically to Design for Decks; do not add a separate $40M or imply sole causation.</td><td>00:46–00:48; 01:40–01:41</td></tr><tr><td>Calculator</td><td>Dedicated calc.html page, prominently linked. Add task, people, hours and hourly value. Use time-based aspirations without inventing travel or purchase prices.</td><td>01:43–01:44; 01:49–01:50</td></tr><tr><td>Call to action</td><td>Sticky navigation CTA and short three-step support beneath the final call button, drawing from Etan’s V1 discussion. Keep the call at 30 minutes.</td><td>01:39–01:42</td></tr><tr><td>Cut</td><td>Homepage FAQ, full embedded calculator, repetitive “three disciplines” headings and the old generic how-we-work block.</td><td>01:41–01:43; 02:04</td></tr></tbody></table></div><section class="review-notes"><h2>Still needed for launch</h2><ul><li><b>Real headshots and introduction video.</b> Etan’s supplied portrait is in place. A verified Zorba portrait is still needed; his initials remain an explicit placeholder.</li><li><b>Final logo assets and attribution.</b> The transcript supports using prior-work names. The seven supplied image files are in place with prominent previous-work attribution.</li><li><b>Booking destination.</b> Buttons open a clearly labeled preview brief. Connect the agreed calendar, verify a real booking and add the appropriate privacy details.</li><li><b>Final copy sign-off.</b> New e-commerce/AI headlines, forest-green palette and periodic-element identity are implementation proposals. Etan’s Claude V1 was interpreted from your spoken review; the underlying Canvas file wasn’t available in this run.</li><li><b>Final verification.</b> See the revision report for completed checks. A real booking test remains blocked until a calendar is supplied.</li></ul><p>Pricing, percentage residuals and contract terms remain off the site: those were exploratory and not agreed as public offers. The live site is public. This revision is held for review and has not been published.</p></section><section class="review-editor"><h2>Try a copy adjustment</h2><p>These edits preview in this browser only. They do not change the published source or sync with Etan. Export your changes and notes together for the next revision.</p><form id="copyEditor"></form><div class="review-actions"><button class="button" id="saveCopy">Save local copy preview</button><button class="button secondary" id="resetCopy">Reset local copy</button></div><p id="editStatus" role="status"></p></section><section class="review-notes"><h2>Leave a section note</h2><form id="noteForm"><label for="reviewer">Your name</label><input id="reviewer" required maxlength="80" placeholder="Zorba or Etan"><label for="sectionName">Section</label><select id="sectionName"><option>Hero & headline</option><option>Growth blockers</option><option>Services & animation</option><option>Previous-work names & proof</option><option>Founders</option><option>Calculator</option><option>Call to action</option><option>Overall design</option></select><label for="reviewNote">What should change?</label><textarea id="reviewNote" rows="4" required maxlength="3000"></textarea><button class="button">Save note in this browser</button></form><div id="savedNotes" aria-live="polite"></div><button class="button secondary" id="exportReview">Export copy changes and notes</button><p class="micro">This is a local review aid, not a shared comment system. No feedback is sent automatically.</p></section></main>'''+footer+modal+script
